{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9vkuXcqgH941kvhrTKe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The recovery middleware now treats a panic with `http.ErrAbortHandler` the same way it treats a broken pipe. It logs one short line with no stack trace, doesn't write a 500, records the error on the context and aborts the request. The check uses `errors.Is`, so a wrapped `ErrAbortHandler` is caught too. The change is in `recovery.go`, and I added `TestPanicWithAbortHandler` to `recovery_test.go`. The recovery tests pass and gofmt is clean.\n\nThat one short log line is still written. If you want it fully silent, it's a one-line change. I haven't committed anything; you're on a detached HEAD."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":716,"cache_read_input_tokens":34363,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":716,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c504ce8d-4c8f-42a5-841d-2b7a58389684","uuid":"2e11e5a8-d3b0-4c0e-9179-2bf62695e962","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:19:39.642Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9vkuHymuYwMjuGjagtx"}
